            <h2>Train Duration, Distance, and Travel Time Overview</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Baltimore to Newark covers roughly 163 miles (263 km) along the busy Northeast Corridor, linking two of the East Coast’s most important transit points. Although this isn’t a high‑speed rail corridor like in Europe, Amtrak’s Acela and Northeast Regional trains offer a steady and pleasant pace, often making the trip more enjoyable than a long drive.</p>
